<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="SRFR-037" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>RegardingResolver title styling v1.3.2 → v1.3.3 (font-weight 400 → 600 per actual OOB DevTools inspection + reduce top padding to match OOB section-header alignment)</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-effort>1h</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort>~35min</actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started>2026-07-03</started>
    <completed>2026-07-03</completed>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>—</parallel-group>
    <tags>pcf,regarding-resolver,fluent-ui,react,styling,version-bump,wave-3-followon,deploy</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-035</depends-on>
    <wave>3</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Out-of-plan follow-on to SRFR-035 (v1.3.2 deploy). Owner post-UAT DevTools
inspection of the OOB "TRACKING" section header revealed actual CSS classes:

  .pa-nn { padding: 4px 0px; }
  .pa-nl { font-size: 14px; }
  .pa-hw { font-weight: 600; }         /* ← 600, NOT 400 as SRFR-034 briefing stated */
  .pa-de { font-family: "Segoe UI", "Segoe UI Web (West European)",
           -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif; }
  .pa-s  { color: rgb(36, 36, 36); }   /* = #242424 */

Font-family, font-size, color, and padding are already correct in v1.3.2.
Font-weight is wrong (currently 400) — must be 600 for OOB parity.

Second issue: owner reports "the Related Record title needs less top padding".
The PCF's root container currently uses `padding: tokens.spacingHorizontalS`
(which is 8px on all sides via Fluent v9 tokens). Compared to OOB section
headers that only carry `.pa-nn { padding: 4px 0px }`, the PCF has ~8px of
extra top padding. Reduce the root container's top padding so the "RELATED
RECORD" title sits at approximately the same visual top offset as the OOB
"TRACKING" section header.

Scope (all in `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/`):

1. `RegardingResolverApp.tsx`:
   - `title` Griffel style block: change `fontWeight: 400` → `fontWeight: 600`.
   - Verify font-family, font-size (14px), color (#242424), padding (4px 0px)
     are already correct — leave unchanged.
   - `container` Griffel style block: replace uniform `padding: tokens.spacingHorizontalS`
     with directional padding to reduce top spacing. Set `paddingTop: 0` and
     keep `paddingRight`/`paddingBottom`/`paddingLeft` at
     `tokens.spacingHorizontalS` (8px) for existing spacing on the other sides.
   - Docstring header: bump v1.3.2 references to v1.3.3, add a "v1.3.3
     (SRFR-037 title-styling fix)" section describing the two changes.

2. Version bump v1.3.2 → v1.3.3 across all 7 anchors per SRFR-033's checklist:
   - ControlManifest.Input.xml (control root version attr)
   - index.ts CONTROL_VERSION
   - RegardingResolverApp.tsx BUILD_DATE (leave as 2026-07-03 if same day)
   - Solution/solution.xml <Version>
   - Solution Control Manifest version attr
   - package.json version
   - Solution/pack.ps1 $version

3. Tests:
   - Bulk grep + replace `1.3.2` → `1.3.3` in test file.
   - Add 1 new test asserting the title element's computed `fontWeight` style
     is `600` (or asserting the makeStyles-emitted CSS resolves to 600).
     Griffel emits atomic class names; the test can grep the title element's
     className or use `window.getComputedStyle(el).fontWeight === '600'`.
   - Optional: assert root container's `paddingTop` is 0 (may be brittle in
     jsdom because Griffel atomic classes require the stylesheet to be
     mounted — skip if the assertion is fragile).

4. Step 9.5 quality gates: `/code-review` + `/adr-check` + `npm run build:prod`.

5. Deploy: pack solution, `pac solution import --force-overwrite`, verify via
   `pac solution list`.

Coordination: SRFR-038 (sprk_todo FormXml fix) running in parallel — different
files, no collision.

Constraints:
  - ADR-022 virtual pattern preserved.
  - SRFR-034/035 features preserved (refresh button, auto-refresh,
    showVersionFooter, PolymorphicPicker consumption unchanged).
  - Path A exception on ADR-021 for OOB parity styling — DOCUMENTED
    exception remains; this task tightens compliance with the ACTUAL OOB
    styles (font-weight 600), not loosens it.
  - Backward compat: no breaking manifest property changes.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>PCF developer familiar with Spaarke PCF version discipline (`src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md`), Fluent v9 Griffel + tokens (`ADR-021`), virtual PCF platform-library pattern (`ADR-022`), shared PolymorphicPicker (`ADR-012`), and Dataverse OOB section-header styling conventions.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
RegardingResolver v1.3.3 deployed to spaarkedev1, verified via
`pac solution list`. Row-1 title "RELATED RECORD" renders with actual OOB
section-header styling: font-weight 600 (semi-bold), font-family Segoe UI
stack, font-size 14px, color #242424, padding 4px 0px. Root container top
padding reduced so the title's visual top offset matches OOB section
headers on the same form. Manual refresh button (SRFR-034), auto-refresh
(SRFR-035), showVersionFooter, PolymorphicPicker consumption all preserved.
All 7 version anchors bumped 1.3.2 → 1.3.3. Tests updated with 1 new
font-weight assertion. `npm run build:prod` passes. ADR-021/022/012
preserved. Backward compat: existing v1.3.2 form bindings continue to
function.
  ]]></goal>

